        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "d43d82e1-2754-5d56-9973-7c8ce518d426",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: The Lost Tomb of Jesus\n- People: Jesus, Mary Magdalene, Judah\n- Places: Jerusalem\n- Concepts: Ossuary, temporary grave, skeletal remains\n\nFacts:\n- In 1980, ossuaries discovered in Jerusalem were later cited by the 2007 documentary \"The Lost Tomb of Jesus.\"\n- The 2007 documentary \"The Lost Tomb of Jesus\" proposed that evidence showed Jesus was married to Mary Magdalene and that their son was named Judah.\n- An ossuary is a chest, box, building, well, or site made to serve as the final resting place of human skeletal remains.\n- In the burial process described for an ossuary, a body is first buried in a temporary grave.\n- In the burial process described for an ossuary, the skeletal remains are removed after some years and placed in an ossuary.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "059e7211-063f-5798-b26c-415f1640a0e1",
        "text": "Page: Jesus bloodline. Sentence: The 2007 documentary \"The Lost Tomb of Jesus\" proposed that evidence existed to show that Jesus was married to Mary Magdalene and that their son was named Judah, based upon inscriptions found on ossuaries discovered in Jerusalem in 1980.\nPage: Ossuary. Sentence: An ossuary is a chest, box, building, well, or site made to serve as the final resting place of human skeletal remains.\nPage: Ossuary. Sentence: A body is first buried in a temporary grave, then after some years the skeletal remains are removed and placed in an ossuary.",
